  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Stregthening Climate Services for Enhanced Climate Resiliance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for capacity development of the regional and national meteorological organsiations. The Project&apos;s expected effect(s) on society is: Improved climate resilience for vulnerable 
populations. 


The expected effects for the target group of the Project are: 

Outcome 1: Stakeholders use climate services for informed actions for Food and Agricultural
 Security (FAS) and Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR) for programs and activities for climate
 change adaptation and preparedness.

Outcome 2: Regional Climate Centers have improved technical solutions for the delivery of 
climate services.

Outcome 3: Improved seasonable climate forecasts and climate services.

Outcome 4: NMHSs (national metrological and hydrological services) have enhanced
knowledge on climate data management and climate services communication to ensure efficient
 delivery and use.

Outcome 5: NORCAP experts have improved capacity to promote best practices in the field.

Outcome 6: Communities and stakeholders are better engaged in the co-developing adaptation 
solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
